not responsible for the spontaneous ordering. They
can remove, however, the degeneracy of different
ordered ground states related by symmetries of the
non-relativistic Hamiltonian. The resulting magnetic
anisotropy energy can facilitate the stability of ordered
ground states at discrete orientations of spins which

